use std
into sdf_ttf.amni

Imports: std, math, gfx, ttf, gfx.sdf_font. No namespace (the names start with sdf_ttf_ or sdf_use_). It lets the SDF text of gfx.sdf_font draw a real TrueType font instead of its built-in stroke font, using the same atlas layout, so sdf_text, sdf_text_w and the hud need no other change. The sdf_font globals it fills are `SDF_ADV` and `SDF_OFF` (fixed arrays of 95 f32, one per ASCII code 32 to 126), `SDF_KERN` (growable f32 list), `SDF_TTF_PIX` (growable byte list), `SDF_READY` (bool) and `SDF_TEX` (gfx::Texture); the atlas constants are `SDF_ATLAS_W` (1024), `SDF_ATLAS_H` (512), `SDF_CELL` (48), `SDF_COLS` (20), `SDF_CAP_H` (24.0, cap height in cell units) and `SDF_SPREAD` (6.0).

`sdf_ttf_dt(g, w, h)` (g: a growable f32 list passed by reference, w and h ints) turns g (w times h values, row major, 0 at feature pixels and 1e20 elsewhere) into the squared Euclidean distance to the nearest feature pixel, in place, with the Felzenszwalb and Huttenlocher 1D lower envelope transform run down every column and then along every row (scratch lists f, d and v of max(w, h) values and z of max(w, h) plus 1, allocated once per call).

`sdf_use_ttf(bytes) bool` (bytes: a read-only byte slice) loads a TrueType font from its file bytes and returns false when it is not one: info is a ttf::Info with d a copy of bytes; info.fo = ttf::font_offset(bytes, 0) and return false when it is below 0 or ttf::init(info) fails. Let cap be the top (y1) of the glyph box of "H" from ttf::gbox (for glyph ttf::glyph_index(info, 72)), or 70 percent of the ascent (x of ttf::vmetrics) when that box is missing or not above 0. U = SDF_CAP_H over cap (cell units per font unit), Q = 4 (hi-res samples per cell unit), S = U times Q, C = SDF_CELL times Q (the hi-res cell side), pen x 8 times Q and baseline y 35 times Q. The atlas pix is SDF_ATLAS_W times SDF_ATLAS_H times 4 zero bytes. For each k from 0 to 94: g = glyph index of code k plus 32; SDF_ADV[k] = x of ttf::hmetrics(info, g) times U; SDF_OFF[k] = 0. Skip to the next k when k is 0 or g is 0. b = ttf::bbox(info, g, S, S, 0.0, 0.0); gw = b.x1 minus b.x0, gh = b.y1 minus b.y0; skip when either is not above 0. cov is gw times gh zero bytes filled by ttf::glyph_bitmap(info, cov, 0, gw, gh, gw, S, S, g). A hi-res pixel (X, Y) of the C by C cell is inside when the cov value at column X minus pen x minus b.x0 and row Y minus baseline y minus b.y0 is in range and at least 128. Build two C by C grids: fin (0 where inside, 1e20 elsewhere) and fout (0 where not inside, 1e20 elsewhere), and run sdf_ttf_dt on both. Then for every cell pixel cx, cy from 0 to SDF_CELL minus 1: X = cx times Q plus 2, Y = cy times Q plus 2; the signed distance in cell units d is minus (square root of fout at X, Y minus 0.5) over Q when (X, Y) is inside, else (square root of fin at X, Y minus 0.5) over Q. The regular value is clamp(0.5 minus (d minus 0.35) over (2 times SDF_SPREAD), 0, 1) and the bold value the same with d minus 1.25. The atlas column is k modulo SDF_COLS and the row k divided by SDF_COLS; the regular value goes at atlas pixel (column times SDF_CELL plus cx, row times SDF_CELL plus cy) and the bold value at the same place with row plus 5, each as round(value times 255) in all four bytes. After the glyphs, SDF_KERN gets 95 times 95 values: entry a times 95 plus b is ttf::kern(info, glyph of a plus 32, glyph of b plus 32) times U. Finally SDF_TTF_PIX becomes pix; when SDF_READY is true call gfx::update_texture(SDF_TEX, pix as a slice). Return true.

`sdf_use_ttf_file(path) bool` (path: a read-only byte slice) reads the file with the built-in read_file(path, buf) into a growable byte list and returns false when that fails, else sdf_use_ttf of the bytes.
